module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ImageSubsheafUniversal
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.RingedToposModulesPullbackTopos
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulPullback
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.PushforwardCommutesCompletion

/-!
# The ideal sheaf `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` of a general sheaf of ideals

Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed sites and let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` be a sheaf of
ideals. Section 52.7 of the Stacks Project, and with it [Stacks, Tags 0A0G and 0A0I], take the
completion on the source along the ideal sheaf `ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` that the source *constructs*
out of `ℐ`. This file makes that construction at an arbitrary `ℐ`, as the image of the canonical
map `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'`, and proves that it satisfies the relation of [Stacks, Tag 099J] to `ℐ`, which
is the hypothesis every statement about the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] carries.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealMap`: the canonical map `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'`, namely
  `f^*` of the inclusion `ℐ ↪ 𝒪` followed by the comparison
  `SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit` of `f^*𝒪` with `𝒪'`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf`: **`ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`**, the image
  subsheaf of that map, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homEquiv_inverseImageIdealMap`: the adjunct of `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'`
  under `f^* ⊣ f_*` is `ℐ ↪ 𝒪 ⟶ f_*𝒪'`, the inclusion followed by `f^♯`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealMap_val_app_unit`: consequently, on sections,
  the map carries the image under the adjunction unit of a section `s` of `ℐ` over `W` to
  `f^♯(s)` over `u(W)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushforwardIdealCompatible_inverseImageIdealSheaf`: **`f^♯`
  carries `f^{-1}ℐ` into `ℐ'`**, that is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.PushforwardIdealCompatible f ℐ ℐ'` holds for this `ℐ'`, with no
  hypothesis on `ℐ` and none on the morphism. This is the input that
  `PushforwardCommutesCompletion.lean` and everything built on it require, and it is what makes
  `ℐ'` the right object: the relation is *false* for a general sheaf of ideals satisfying no
  constraint, and *trivially true* for `ℐ' = 𝒪'`, so only a constructed `ℐ'` carries content.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_le` and
  `.inverseImageIdealSheaf_le_iff`: **`ℐ'` is the *least* sheaf of ideals of `𝒪'` receiving
  `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ)`.** With the previous item this is the defining property Section 52.7 asks of
  `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`, so it identifies this construction with every other one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_pullbackTopos`: [Stacks, Tag 03DO] for the clause
  [Stacks, Tag 03DL] (5) at the site-presented pullback — `f^*` preserves finite type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf`: **`ℐ'` is of finite type
  when `ℐ` is**, which is what makes the derived completion functor along `ℐ'` exist by
  [Stacks, Tag 099F].

## Implementation notes

The leastness of `ℐ'` is the universal property of the image,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_le`, read through the adjunction
`f^* ⊣ f_*`: see the docstring of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_le`.

*Why the compatibility is an adjunction computation and not a membership check.* `f^*` of a
sheaf of modules is a colimit followed by a sheafification, so a section of `f^*ℐ` over an
object of the source site is not presented by anything; in particular `f^♯(s)` is not visibly in
the pointwise range of `f^*ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'`. What is available is the adjunction unit
`ℐ ⟶ f_*f^*ℐ`, whose value over `W` is a section of `f^*ℐ` over `u(W)` by the definition of the
direct image. Applying the map to *that* section is, by
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.homEquiv_unit`, the same as applying the adjunct of the map; and the
adjunct is computed by `homEquiv_inverseImageIdealMap`, using
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left` and the defining property
`SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction_homEquiv_pullbackObjUnitToUnit` of the comparison
`f^*𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'`. So the section lies in the *pointwise* range, which is stronger than the local
membership the image asks for.

*Relation to the globally generated case.* When `ℐ = (t_1, …, t_s)` is generated by finitely
many global sections and the two sites have terminal objects matched by `u`,
`PushforwardCommutesCompletionConstructedIdeal.lean` builds `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` instead as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` of the transported family
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushGlobalSections`, and the theorem names there carry
`inverseImageIdealSheaf` as a suffix for that object. The two constructions **agree**, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_generatedIdealSheaf` of
`InverseImageIdealSheafSlice.lean`. The identification does not need `f^*ℐ` to be generated by
the pulled-back generators: both constructions are characterised as the least sheaf of ideals of
`𝒪'` receiving `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ)` — for the one here by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_le_iff` and for the other by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_generatedIdealSheaf_pushGlobalSections` — and a universal
property determines its object. Nothing below depends on the identification, and nothing below
is restricted to the globally generated case.

Deliberately untagged: this is the construction of the ideal sheaf the display of Section 52.7
is about, not a statement of the Stacks Project. [Stacks, Tag 099J] itself is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete`, which consumes the relation
proved here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
